{
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "def_name": "modular_agent_std::ui::NoteModule",
      "configs": {
        "note": "# AutoGUI showcase\n\nStart the patch, then press a **Unit Input** on the left. Every row sends real keyboard and mouse input to the desktop.\n\n- **Row 1 — Mouse Position**: reads the cursor position, and its offset in the window under it.\n- **Row 2 — GUI Action** (Windows only): opens Notepad with Win+R and types into it. The Object Input holds the action array; each action is one step, run in order with `pause_ms` between them.\n- **Row 3 — Type Text → Hotkey**: after a 3-second Delay, types the text into whatever has focus, then presses `shift+home` to select the typed line. Click into a text editor during the delay.\n\n- **Row 4 — Move Mouse → Mouse Position → Click → Hotkey**: glides the mouse 200 px right over half a second, reads where it landed, right-clicks there to open a context menu, then closes it with `esc`.\n- **Row 5 — Find Window → Click → Type Text** (Windows only, run Row 2 first): finds Notepad, fixes its text area at 800×600 logical pixels, clicks the middle of it and types a line.\n\n**Abort**: move the mouse into a screen corner to stop a running sequence (`failsafe`).\n\n**Edit while stopped**: a Text Input or Object Input sends its value as soon as it is edited while the patch is running, which would fire the input right away."
      },
      "config_specs": {
        "note": {
          "value": "",
          "type": "markdown",
          "hide_title": true
        }
      },
      "x": -760,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 620
    },
